  "text": {
    "intro": "The Inverlaig ferry runs a full day of crossings in theory, and a variable number in practice.\nFive skippers are involved. Determine each skipper's start time, vessel and reason.\n- **Skipper**: Calla, Eilidh, Tormod, Senga and Ruaridh.\n- **Start time** (listed from earlier to later): 8am, 9am, 10am, 11am and noon.\n- **Vessel**: the Ailsa Belle, the Tern, the Broch Maid, the Siller Grey and the Steadfast.\n- **Delay blamed on**: fog, a missing deckhand, a fouled propeller, paperwork and a passenger's dog.\nEvery skipper has a different start time, vessel and reason, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The skipper who commands the Siller Grey sails at 10am.",
      "The skipper who blames a passenger's dog falls somewhere between Eilidh and Ruaridh in start time order. Eilidh commands the Steadfast.",
      "Eilidh blames a missing deckhand.",
      "The skipper who blames a fouled propeller and 9am are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The skipper who commands the Steadfast and 9am are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "9am is exactly one hour earlier than Tormod, with no start time in between.",
      "10am falls somewhere between Eilidh and Senga in start time order.",
      "The skipper who blames paperwork falls somewhere between the skipper who commands the Siller Grey and the skipper who commands the Steadfast in start time order.",
      "Ruaridh and the skipper who commands the Broch Maid are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The skipper who commands the Tern is earlier than the skipper who blames fog in start time order."
    ]
  }
